# A gate-level netlist of soc_top that keeps the RTL's net names.
#
# The ORFS netlist cannot be used for module-level equivalence checking. Its
# synthesis flattens and then lets ABC rename, so a register the RTL calls
# `addr_reg` survives only as a `$scopeinfo` annotation and not as a wire.
# EQY matches gold to gate by wire name, finds no internal match point, and is
# left proving a whole module as one partition with all of its state unmatched
# -- which for anything holding an accumulator is unprovable by induction at
# any depth. Measured on mem_axi_slave: UNPROVEN against the ORFS netlist at
# depth 5 and again at depth 20, PROVED_EQUIVALENT in 9.0s against this one.
#
# Hierarchy is kept on purpose. The sweep proves one module at a time, so a
# flat netlist would be both slower to produce and useless to it.
read_verilog -lib macros/macro_blackbox_stubs.v
read_verilog bench/rtl/*.v
hierarchy -top soc_top
synth -top soc_top
dfflibmap -liberty sta/sky130hd/sky130_fd_sc_hd__tt_025C_1v80.lib
abc -liberty sta/sky130hd/sky130_fd_sc_hd__tt_025C_1v80.lib
opt_clean
stat
write_verilog -noattr artifacts/synth/soc_top_named.v
